# BENCH LIGHT — THE GARAGE, the hub.
#
# SECOND TAKE, and the first one is worth naming because it was the obvious
# read and it was wrong: a music box picking out a lullaby in C major. Sweet,
# twee, and about a man who does not exist. THIS man drives through a crowd at
# a hundred and twenty and files it under road surface; he is not sentimental,
# he is CONTENT. He has spent ten years of weekends building a spaceship out
# here and he is good at it.
#
# So the garage is not a lullaby. It is a WORKSHOP AT ONE IN THE MORNING with
# somebody competent in it — the only score in the game with nothing hunting
# you, and the one the player hears for longer than any other, because this is
# where the shopping, the errands and the bench are.
#
# THREE DECISIONS.
#
#   IT IS A GROOVE, AND THE BASS IS THE TUNE'S EQUAL. A syncopated 3+3+2 hook
#   that runs the whole track and is the thing you would actually hum. A hub
#   theme that merely sits there is a hub theme the player mutes.
#
#   A DORIAN, WHICH IS THE MODE FOR UNBOTHERED. Minor, but with a natural
#   SIXTH — the F♯ — and the whole piece leans on it: it is the one bright note
#   in a dark room, it lands held at the end of every phrase, and it is the
#   last thing left playing in the hush. Nothing about this room is sad.
#
#   IT NEVER GETS HOME. Every section ends on D7, the chord one step short of
#   the A minor it keeps promising, and hands straight back to the vamp. The
#   piece circles happily for two minutes and never once resolves — which is
#   the ship on the lawn, and nobody in the game mentions that either.
#
# AND NO KIT AT ALL. The only percussion is the bench: a wrench set down, a tin
# knocked over, on a four-bar grid that never lands on a downbeat. Somebody is
# working. They are not keeping time.
#
# THERE IS NO PAD EITHER, and that was a deliberate cut rather than an omission.
# One was written and the sheet showed it sitting in the same octave as the
# keys, two square voices in each other's way — and it was the quietest thing in
# the piece, so cutting it rather than re-voicing it lost nothing and left four
# parts that each own a register: hook, comp, tune, bench.
#
# Compile:  node scripts/song-import.mjs content/songs/bench_light.song --sheet

id     bench_light
title  BENCH LIGHT
tempo  92
about
  A workshop at one in the morning with somebody competent in it — the hub, and
  the only score in the game with nothing hunting you. A syncopated bass hook
  carries it rather than a melody sitting on top, the mode is A DORIAN so the
  bright natural sixth is the note everything leans on, and every section ends
  one chord short of home and hands straight back to the vamp: it circles for
  two minutes, happily, and never resolves. There is no kit — the only
  percussion is a wrench set down and a tin knocked over, four bars apart and
  never on a downbeat. Original melodies; nothing sampled.

# ── THE CAST ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE HOOK. Written out longhand every bar, because this is the part of the
# piece a figure could not have written: it is the tune, it just happens to be
# at the bottom.
voice bass   triangle vol=.058 gate=.8
# The bench radio's electric piano — seventh chords on the off-beats, warm and
# a little out of tune, sitting in the gap between the bass and the lead.
voice keys   square vol=.016 gate=.5 attack=25 detune=8 pan=-0.2 echo=.3
# The line over the top. A TRIANGLE, not a sine — woody rather than glassy,
# which is the whole difference between a workbench and a nursery.
voice lead   triangle vol=.042 gate=.7 attack=20 echo=.4 vib=4.5/10/280

# ── THE BENCH ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
drum  wrench noise vol=.014 gate=.1 bp=1900 pan=.35
drum  tin    noise vol=.011 gate=.08 lp=1000 pan=-0.3

# ── INTRO — the hook, alone, and then the lamp ─────────────────────────────
section intro
  chords Am7 | D7 | Am7 | D7
  bass   a2*3 a2*3 c3*2 e3*4 d3*2 c3*2 | d2*3 d2*3 f#2*2 a2*4 g2*2 f#2*2
         a2*3 a2*3 c3*2 e3*4 d3*2 c3*2 | d2*3 d2*3 f#2*2 a2*4 g2*4
  keys   .*16 | .*16 | offbeat:3 | offbeat:3
  lead   .*16 | .*16 | .*16 | .*4 f#4*4 a4*4 c5*4
  wrench ................|..........x.....|................|.....x..........
  tin    ................|................|.......x........|................

# ── A — the vamp. Bar 8 hands back to bar 1 and never lands on A minor ─────
section a
  chords Am7 | D7 | Am7 | D7 | Cmaj7 | Bm7 | Am7 | D7
  bass   a2*3 a2*3 c3*2 e3*4 d3*2 c3*2 | d2*3 d2*3 f#2*2 a2*4 g2*2 f#2*2
         a2*3 a2*3 c3*2 e3*4 d3*2 c3*2 | d2*3 d2*3 f#2*2 a2*4 g2*2 f#2*2
         c3*3 c3*3 e3*2 g3*4 e3*2 d3*2 | b2*3 b2*3 d3*2 f#3*4 e3*2 d3*2
         a2*3 a2*3 c3*2 e3*4 d3*2 c3*2 | d2*3 d2*3 f#2*2 a2*4 g2*4
  lead   .*4 a4*4 c5*4 e5*4 | d5*8 c5*4 a4*4 | .*4 c5*2 d5*2 e5*4 g5*4 | f#5*8 e5*8
         e5*4 g5*4 a5*8 | g5*4 f#5*4 d5*8 | e5*4 c5*4 a4*8 | .*4 f#4*4 a4*4 c5*4
  keys   offbeat 3
  wrench ................|..........x.....|................|.....x..........
  tin    ................|................|.......x........|................

# ── B — the ship. It walks down out of the vamp, gets higher, comes back ───
section b
  chords Cmaj7 | G | Fmaj7 | Em7 | Dm7 | Em7 | Fmaj7 | D7
  bass   c3*3 c3*3 e3*2 g3*4 e3*2 c3*2 | g2*3 g2*3 b2*2 d3*4 b2*2 g2*2
         f2*3 f2*3 a2*2 c3*4 a2*2 f2*2 | e2*3 e2*3 g2*2 b2*4 a2*2 g2*2
         d2*3 d2*3 f2*2 a2*4 g2*2 f2*2 | e2*3 e2*3 g2*2 b2*4 d3*2 b2*2
         f2*3 f2*3 a2*2 c3*4 e3*2 c3*2 | d2*3 d2*3 f#2*2 a2*4 g2*4
  lead   g5*4 e5*4 c5*8 | d5*4 b4*4 g4*8 | a4*4 c5*4 f5*8 | e5*8 d5*8
         d5*4 f5*4 a5*8 | b5*4 a5*4 g5*8 | a5*8 e5*8 | f#5*4 e5*4 d5*8
  keys   offbeat 3
  wrench ................|..........x.....|................|.....x..........
  tin    ................|................|.......x........|................

# ── HUSH — the radio off. Half the bass, four notes, and the sixth left
#    ringing on its own at the end of it ───────────────────────────────────
section hush
  chords Am7 | Am7 | Fmaj7 | Fmaj7 | Cmaj7 | Cmaj7 | D7 | D7
  bass   a2*8 e3*8 | a2*8 c3*8 | f2*8 c3*8 | f2*8 a2*8
         c3*8 g2*8 | c3*8 e3*8 | d2*8 a2*8 | d2*8 f#2*8
  lead   .*16 | .*16 | .*8 a4*8 | c5*8 .*8
         .*16 | g5*8 e5*8 | .*8 d5*8 | f#5*8 .*8
  wrench ................|..........x.....|................|.....x..........
  tin    ................|................|.......x........|................

# ── CLOSE — the hook one more time, and the seam is not a cadence ─────────
section close
  chords Am7 | D7 | Cmaj7 | D7
  bass   a2*3 a2*3 c3*2 e3*4 d3*2 c3*2 | d2*3 d2*3 f#2*2 a2*4 g2*2 f#2*2
         c3*8 e3*8 | d2*8 .*8
  lead   e5*4 c5*4 a4*8 | .*16 | e5*8 g5*8 | f#5*8 .*8
  keys   offbeat:3 | offbeat:3 | offbeat:3 | .*16
  wrench ................|..........x.....|................|................
  tin    ................|................|.......x........|................

order  intro a b a hush b close
